> One D & D characteristic that hasn't made it into nethack yet is age.
> [... comments deleted ...]

Don't you think if a warrior, attempting to find the Amulet of Yendor
(it's local legend, you know), would start at the prime of his life (early
20s)?  If that was the case, I don't think a full game, to hell and back,
would take the 50 or so years needed to die of old age.  It sure would be
a bogus way to die, also, what the game doesn't need is a way of dying that
you don't have much control over (suddenly the game is dependant on finding
the potion of youth).

It does seem like a certain amount of time passes, because your pets eventually
grow to be large, but that takes quite a while, and spending 50 years/game
is unreasonable, with the current tempo.
